% Test cases for the commodes policy (commodes.le): synthetic claims, one
% per situation and criterion of LCD L33736 and per benefit point of Policy
% Article A52461. Findings are recorded as the treating practitioner's, a
% medical reviewer's or the Council's; a finding nobody made leaves the
% answer conditional. A commode is a purchase: no rental month.

the target language is: prolog.

the knowledge base commodes cases includes these resources:
    commodes.

the knowledge base commodes cases includes:

query pay is:
    which claim is payable.

query rn is:
    which claim is reasonable and necessary.

query stage is:
    the query fails at which section.

query flip is:
    which minimal change to the scenario makes it the case that
        claim 1 is payable.

% A complete claim for a stationary commode chair (E0163) for a beneficiary
% confined to a single room: the standard written order communicated before
% the date of service, the delivery and its proof.
scenario single_room_complete is:
    claim 1 is for the commode.
    the HCPCS code of the commode is "E0163".
    the commode is furnished to Ann.
    the residence of Ann is private residence.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2026-03-01.
    Ann is confined to a single room.
    the order for the commode is dated 2026-02-20.
    the order for the commode is signed by the treating practitioner.
    the order for the commode includes beneficiary name.
    the order for the commode includes order date.
    the order for the commode includes description of the item.
    the order for the commode includes quantity to be dispensed.
    the order for the commode includes treating practitioner name.
    the order for the commode was communicated to the supplier on 2026-02-22.
    the commode was delivered on 2026-03-01.
    the supplier holds proof of delivery for the commode.
    pay expects answers ["claim 1 is payable"].
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].
    stage expects answers [].

% The other two situations: confined to one level with no toilet on it
% (claim 1); confined to the home with no toilet facilities in it (claim 2);
% and confined to one level of a home whose toilet is on that level (claim
% 3): not incapable of using it.
scenario levels_and_homes is:
    claim 1 is for the first commode.
    the HCPCS code of the first commode is "E0163".
    the first commode is furnished to Ben.
    Ben is confined to one level of the home.
    the level of the home to which Ben is confined has no toilet.
    claim 2 is for the second commode.
    the HCPCS code of the second commode is "E0163".
    the second commode is furnished to Cy.
    Cy is confined to the home.
    the home of Cy has no toilet facilities.
    claim 3 is for the third commode.
    the HCPCS code of the third commode is "E0163".
    the third commode is furnished to Dee.
    Dee is confined to one level of the home.
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary", "claim 2 is reasonable and necessary"].

% The commode criterion fails: nothing in the record confines the
% beneficiary — the query fails at the question.
scenario not_confined is:
    claim 1 is for the commode.
    the HCPCS code of the commode is "E0163".
    the commode is furnished to Eve.
    the residence of Eve is private residence.
    rn expects answers [].
    stage expects answers ["the query fails at question"].

% Detachable arms (E0165): with the finding, covered; the Council finds the
% record shows no need for the feature.
scenario detachable_arms is:
    claim 1 is for the commode.
    the HCPCS code of the commode is "E0165".
    the commode is furnished to Fay.
    Fay is confined to a single room.
    the finding detachable arms necessary about Fay is established, according to the treating practitioner, because "lateral transfers from the wheelchair require the arm removed".
    claim 2 is for the second commode.
    the HCPCS code of the second commode is "E0165".
    the second commode is furnished to Gus.
    Gus is confined to a single room.
    the finding detachable arms necessary about Gus is unsupported, according to the Council, because "the record shows the beneficiary standing to transfer with a caregiver and is silent on body configuration".
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].

% Weight: an extra wide/heavy duty commode (E0168) for a 280-pound
% beneficiary is not covered; for a 300-pound one it is.
scenario heavy_duty_weight is:
    claim 1 is for the heavy duty commode.
    the HCPCS code of the heavy duty commode is "E0168".
    the heavy duty commode is furnished to Hal.
    Hal is confined to a single room.
    the weight of Hal is 280 pounds.
    claim 2 is for the second heavy duty commode.
    the HCPCS code of the second heavy duty commode is "E0168".
    the second heavy duty commode is furnished to Ida.
    Ida is confined to a single room.
    the weight of Ida is 300 pounds.
    rn expects answers ["claim 2 is reasonable and necessary"].

% A commode with seat lift mechanism (E0170): the commode criterion and the
% four seat lift findings; with one of them unsupported, not covered.
scenario seat_lift_commode is:
    claim 1 is for the lift commode.
    the HCPCS code of the lift commode is "E0170".
    the lift commode is furnished to Jo.
    Jo is confined to a single room.
    the finding qualifying seat lift diagnosis about Jo is established, according to the treating practitioner, because "severe osteoarthritis of both knees".
    the finding seat lift part of course of treatment about Jo is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding completely incapable of standing from any chair about Jo is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding able to ambulate once standing about Jo is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    claim 2 is for the second lift commode.
    the HCPCS code of the second lift commode is "E0171".
    the second lift commode is furnished to Kim.
    Kim is confined to a single room.
    the finding qualifying seat lift diagnosis about Kim is established, according to the treating practitioner, because "severe osteoarthritis of the hip".
    the finding seat lift part of course of treatment about Kim is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding completely incapable of standing from any chair about Kim is unsupported, according to the medical reviewer, because "the record shows the beneficiary rising from an armchair with difficulty".
    the finding able to ambulate once standing about Kim is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].

% A commode chair used as a raised toilet seat over the toilet: noncovered.
scenario used_as_raised_seat is:
    claim 1 is for the commode.
    the HCPCS code of the commode is "E0163".
    the commode is furnished to Lou.
    Lou is confined to a single room.
    the commode is used as a raised toilet seat positioned over the toilet.
    rn expects answers [].

% A footrest (E0175) and a raised toilet seat (E0244): in scope, outside
% the benefit — the claims fail at applicability.
scenario footrest_and_raised_seat is:
    claim 1 is for the footrest.
    the HCPCS code of the footrest is "E0175".
    the footrest is furnished to Ann.
    the residence of Ann is private residence.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2026-03-01.
    claim 2 is for the raised toilet seat.
    the HCPCS code of the raised toilet seat is "E0244".
    the raised toilet seat is furnished to Ann.
    pay expects answers [].
    rn expects answers [].
    stage expects answers ["the query fails at applicability"].

% A replacement pail (E0167) for a covered commode.
scenario replacement_pail is:
    claim 1 is for the pail.
    the HCPCS code of the pail is "E0167".
    the pail is an accessory of the commode.
    the pail is furnished to Ann.
    the HCPCS code of the commode is "E0163".
    the commode is furnished to Ann.
    Ann is confined to a single room.
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].

% Reasonable and necessary, but no proof of delivery: payable fails at the
% remedy.
scenario no_proof_of_delivery is:
    claim 1 is for the commode.
    the HCPCS code of the commode is "E0163".
    the commode is furnished to Ann.
    the residence of Ann is private residence.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2026-03-01.
    Ann is confined to a single room.
    the order for the commode is dated 2026-02-20.
    the order for the commode is signed by the treating practitioner.
    the order for the commode includes beneficiary name.
    the order for the commode includes order date.
    the order for the commode includes description of the item.
    the order for the commode includes quantity to be dispensed.
    the order for the commode includes treating practitioner name.
    the order for the commode was communicated to the supplier on 2026-02-22.
    the commode was delivered on 2026-03-01.
    pay expects answers [].
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].
    stage expects answers ["the query fails at remedy"].
    flip expects changes [["add: the supplier holds proof of delivery for the commode"]].
